values ('c0d1e2f3-4a5b-4c17-8e77-7f8a9b0c1d17', 'orchestration-arranging', 'Orchestration / Arranging', 'This course develops practical and artistic skills in writing for instruments and ensembles. Students study ranges, transpositions, instrumental color, string, woodwind, brass, and percussion writing, full-orchestra scoring, voicing and doubling, texture and color, arranging for varied ensembles, and professional score and parts preparation. The course emphasizes score study, idiomatic playability, listening, notation clarity, digital workflow, revision, and real-world rehearsal usability.');

