"556da3fd-a430-4631-a4b2-7c260a1cd69c", "type": "concept", "title": "F horn"}, {"id": "077012bc-ee47-4a92-8b19-cbd577ef3c32", "type": "concept", "title": "Octave transpositions"}, {"id": "b9b5e66e-9d40-49b3-8248-f3686a9c43b5", "type": "concept", "title": "Concert vs. transposed score"}], "description": "Why learn it: Students practice reading, writing, and checking transpositions across orchestral and band instruments."}, {"id": "6b1ccb7f-3361-4a60-b5ae-f5e63909bcca", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Instrumental notation basics", "children": [{"id": "3692f28c-e57c-43ae-b209-d0f8172d5f58", "type": "concept", "title": "Clefs"}, {"id": "45016368-19cc-452a-ad05-17eb22349bcf", "type": "concept", "title": "Key signatures"}, {"id": "1452c9a3-0393-4808-b614-1cc2a033794a", "type": "concept", "title": "Octave signs"}, {"id": "09451cba-8812-4251-a21f-e43aecd3e411", "type": "concept", "title": "Instrument names"}, {"id": "5f13ec14-98d3-4825-a399-6435e777f169", "type": "concept", "title": "Part labels"}], "description": "Why learn it: Students learn notation conventions that prevent rehearsal confusion."}]}, {"id": "7a306bb5-426c-4967-b80b-f8472430f53d", "type": "topic", "title": "Score Study and Instrumental Listening", "description": "This added topic makes orchestration a listening discipline, not only a notation task. Students study master scores, recordings, and live demonstrations to connect page decisions to sound.", "children": [{"id": "d42dcd3c-bd03-4921-a675-399534d2e3c9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Score-reading habits", "children": [{"id": "b783a398-0a83-43c7-8672-94d80d03356e", "type": "concept", "title": "Score order"}, {"id": "0b0d72e9-c27d-4d69-b990-0cfc604c6d0c", "type": "concept", "title": "Cueing entrances"}, {"id": "72dd1fdc-19b0-4698-9100-66107aa43a3c", "type": "concept", "title": "Condensed reading"}, {"id": "beaeb8da-0f0d-4f59-97d3-809f211e7d98", "type": "concept", "title": "Systems and rehearsal marks"}, {"id": "3bd71fcc-626a-41f8-917a-4064de90df58", "type": "concept", "title": "Score annotation"}], "description": "Why learn it: Students learn to follow full scores efficiently and locate orchestration decisions."}, {"id": "eb4673a0-8d71-4bcf-88fd-358d0a5cb1e2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Timbre recognition", "children": [{"id": "cd08f0cd-ff10-40c5-8ab0-aa15f3716cd4", "type": "concept", "title": "Solo color"}, {"id": "86d55e27-e6b3-4d13-8c17-f5de611ad101", "type": "concept", "title": "Section sound"}, {"id": "f22b9401-03b2-4265-bf7a-bf7ab108060d", "type": "concept", "title": "Register shifts"}, {"id": "63b7c7b4-2a0a-41ad-866d-fc8c4ac4fa66", "type": "concept", "title": "Articulation color"}, {"id": "0166740b-9561-4c87-ab9f-62985d8d2a99", "type": "concept", "title": "Blend vs. contrast"}], "description": "Why learn it: Students build an aural vocabulary for instrumental color and blend."}, {"id": "b7a8016d-e9b5-4b42-a6e8-84899937f655", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Model analysis", "children": [{"id": "17d84c53-f851-42fe-b395-9d5069c6f67c", "type": "concept", "title": "Reduction"}, {"id": "d8bb96a8-333f-4187-9bce-16d27b6ad9ca", "type": "concept", "title": "Doubling map"}, {"id": "24542a6e-efe8-45d6-ac25-e320751b68c0", "type": "concept", "title": "Texture map"}, {"id": "533fe204-969b-44cc-b83d-0800b0872f7c", "type": "concept", "title": "Dynamic plan"}, {"id": "d870a30d-c21a-4ae3-8a01-682ce1d1282a", "type": "concept", "title": "Orchestration timeline"}], "description": "Why learn it: Students learn by reverse-engineering successful orchestral passages."}]}, {"id": "100e7e03-61a3-4a77-ab1d-8b4b1e57eaee", "type": "topic", "title": "String Writing", "description": "Strings are flexible, expressive, and central to many ensembles, but they require idiomatic knowledge. Students learn bowing, divisi, resonance, register, and texture.", "children": [{"id": "4733aae2-8e26-42de-8a65-4642b3fc7f37", "type": "subtopic", "title": "String technique and notation", "children": [{"id": "19bfe84a-99a1-4215-967e-975c1ef91b7f", "type": "concept", "title": "Bowing"}, {"id": "4c1b443e-7cc2-48b9-bf5e-319e938b7574", "type": "concept", "title": "Pizzicato"}, {"id": "5f9622d7-201b-4d00-878e-bd856be04879", "type": "concept", "title": "Double stops"}, {"id": "a46f6ac3-d03b-4164-9c8f-72fa7f0f6572", "type": "concept", "title": "Harmonics"}, {"id": "378f7a54-0684-472e-a431-245de96fdd97", "type": "concept", "title": "Divisi"}], "description": "Why learn it: Students learn the basic vocabulary that makes string parts playable."}, {"id": "39f05095-0258-4724-bc80-1f62ac151314", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Section writing", "children": [{"id": "f27bcf7f-128c-45dd-9838-7a116a0d5a26", "type": "concept", "title": "Violin I/II roles"}, {"id": "8a715e3a-839f-4514-858a-159a4aad31da", "type": "concept", "title": "Viola color"}, {"id": "3bd7fbf7-11f9-4f36-8918-87d6bafafe08", "type": "concept", "title": "Cello melody"}, {"id": "79644bb9-6132-445e-9bc9-4b0f1835d793", "type": "concept", "title": "Bass support"}, {"id": "34d22b31-852e-40d0-aaee-e52ec44cac05", "type": "concept", "title": "Spacing"}], "description": "Why learn it: Students learn to distribute melody, harmony, bass, and inner motion across the string choir."}, {"id": "9d938ea9-e7ad-4edb-b81e-6bbeecaa9cd4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "String textures", "children": [{"id": "556e660d-d751-4d48-ab57-71ab301cbb58", "type": "concept", "title": "Tremolo"}, {"id": "83f49fd2-b158-4eb1-b0e9-0d79edbcbbdb", "type": "concept", "title": "Ostinato"}, {"id": "34ae65d1-5e64-4480-963e-31d28ba59c7a", "type": "concept", "title": "Pads"}, {"id": "b98d6332-13e0-48e4-9c2a-115a4b9b4229", "type": "concept", "title": "Countermelody"}, {"id": "eab95836-b874-4e2c-b34b-b5ca6ba88675", "type": "concept", "title": "Chamber vs. orchestral writing"}], "description": "Why learn it: Students practice creating motion, weight, transparency, and intensity."}]}, {"id": "f1d6339e-11af-4f7c-bee8-10fe826429ec", "type": "topic", "title": "Woodwind Writing", "description": "Woodwinds offer vivid individuality, agility, blend, and color. Students learn to write lines that respect breath, register, finger technique, and timbral identity.", "children": [{"id": "724c229a-2d94-4256-8740-67102068d3b5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Woodwind families and registers", "children": [{"id": "4c07badc-2ded-4f9d-bd9e-805d347d53da", "type": "concept", "title": "Flute and piccolo"}, {"id": "fd7a186f-c67c-45e7-bd8b-d249ba3c3691", "type": "concept", "title": "Oboe and English horn"}, {"id": "8db02dab-5ef4-4398-9c0f-879253e5ee8c", "type": "concept", "title": "Clarinet family"}, {"id": "f6cc30d7-dd9e-47f1-b7a1-0f6ab4d75c8a", "type": "concept", "title": "Bassoon and contrabassoon"}, {"id": "0f9a0903-9c37-4988-bc62-fbd2741d45ea", "type": "concept", "title": "Register breaks"}], "description": "Why learn it: Students learn characteristic colors and practical limits for flute, oboe, clarinet, bassoon, and auxiliaries."}, {"id": "28ca23ad-afd9-4e2f-b506-29775198a455", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Breath and line writing", "children": [{"id": "95ac6755-199c-4b89-9861-d38bfffe5ab1", "type": "concept", "title": "Breath marks"}, {"id": "1b0901c1-8cb8-4d98-92f8-8e721a10cbfc", "type": "concept", "title": "Rest placement"}, {"id": "877c1dc9-ef91-4cb9-b504-0f61bf659cff", "type": "concept", "title": "Sustained lines"}, {"id": "4dac1c9e-4b8c-4781-be94-05f23ea218f3", "type": "concept", "title": "Articulation"}, {"id": "b708cc86-9b86-4d6f-9460-d23cae8ea91b", "type": "concept", "title": "Technical passagework"}], "description": "Why learn it: Students learn to write wind parts that phrase naturally."}, {"id": "719e5e21-de92-4276-bdfe-fb79a0f3ae21", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Color combinations", "children": [{"id": "7fd26c24-f78f-4c14-8c60-5a6c449a51e5", "type": "concept", "title": "Unison color"}, {"id": "21e55bae-ae1a-4c49-92e8-b0cd16c43ec6", "type": "concept", "title": "Octave doubling"}, {"id": "162be389-7d09-4773-8437-a0eb88174561", "type": "concept", "title": "Choir writing"}, {"id": "8ac675fb-bcd2-4e09-969e-addd1c313826", "type": "concept", "title": "Solo handoffs"}, {"id": "b9961d60-e136-4a9b-96aa-2b1e7cdd4eef", "type": "concept", "title": "Mixed timbres"}], "description": "Why learn it: Students practice blending and contrasting woodwinds with each other and with other families."}]}, {"id": "d0903e32-e200-45f5-a9f1-c8b46119ca72", "type": "topic", "title": "Brass Writing", "description": "Brass writing carries power, brilliance, warmth, ceremony, and danger when mishandled. Students learn range, endurance, balance, mutes, articulation, and harmonic spacing.", "children": [{"id": "47fb3952-d52a-4afe-a953-d45d96606e6d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Brass ranges and endurance", "children": [{"id": "a81ff563-a2c1-425a-93c1-df5bb74c795a", "type": "concept", "title": "Trumpet"}, {"id": "f0753155-16a3-4550-9d60-0efcc8c91976", "type": "concept", "title": "Horn"}, {"id": "6a95457b-126d-45a8-899f-ca18d2b1a91d", "type": "concept", "title": "Trombone"}, {"id": "240db8f2-f03f-4ce7-aa42-b19277cef94f", "type": "concept", "title": "Tuba"}, {"id": "d798b746-0068-4d65-aacb-508bf5da4376", "type": "concept", "title": "Fatigue management"}], "description": "Why learn it: Students learn how register, dynamics, rests, and repeated entries affect playability."}, {"id": "4b67b8e0-2a90-481f-830b-c1e8a5fa7548", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Brass choir voicing", "children": [{"id": "94eb993e-7cb4-45d5-bbb6-526d5913dd9a", "type": "concept", "title": "Open spacing"}, {"id": "449c7d0f-f010-44e6-a422-51d48c41f8bf", "type": "concept", "title": "Close spacing"}, {"id": "f5311f90-6899-4a94-9530-af6fcc325dea", "type": "concept", "title": "Horn middle voices"}, {"id": "9a9cfbac-0f79-472c-8c5b-05f728b1b74e", "type": "concept", "title": "Trombone chorales"}, {"id": "4a903fa3-00db-4cad-a505-7c09921ab7bd", "type": "concept", "title": "Bass support"}], "description": "Why learn it: Students practice spacing chords and distributing roles across the brass section."}, {"id": "e6c8e800-4a9a-4474-a087-82f033fb6442", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Color and articulation", "children": [{"id": "324cffa9-3b10-4d75-b903-8e066ee10bc1", "type": "concept", "title": "Mutes"}, {"id": "9358b946-b4d0-4d4a-b553-c05662a58fdd", "type": "concept", "title": "Marcato"}, {"id": "7590f3c1-ff78-4ad2-b49b-0be93d468f69", "type": "concept", "title": "Legato"}, {"id": "90ef8bdc-3430-41dd-8fc6-aa81ae6bd44d", "type": "concept", "title": "Fanfares"}, {"id": "eecc31a2-0303-48c1-a015-6bf030204b6b", "type": "concept", "title": "Soft brass writing"}], "description": "Why learn it: Students learn how brass color changes through mutes, attack, dynamics, and register."}]}, {"id": "89eb5622-68b0-4904-93ad-3fc7a92908f9", "type": "topic", "title": "Percussion", "description": "Percussion expands rhythm, color, emphasis, atmosphere, and theatricality. Students learn practical setup, notation, player logistics, and the difference between coloristic and structural percussion writing.", "children": [{"id": "d5c4ec8f-58e8-411b-8576-67ab409e8dea", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Pitched and unpitched percussion", "children": [{"id": "209eed2f-f0a3-4c03-9cd4-753348793ce8", "type": "concept", "title": "Timpani"}, {"id": "36941e87-24cf-4fdb-a8eb-d15615487735", "type": "concept", "title": "Mallet instruments"}, {"id": "76057292-94e5-42ff-84b3-7f9df95a6b03", "type": "concept", "title": "Drums"}, {"id": "0a3dc425-f1d5-436d-9819-cae5bdf6c58f", "type": "concept", "title": "Cymbals and gongs"}, {"id": "ebd42f0d-789b-4dcf-b24c-a505dba44d3a", "type": "concept", "title": "Accessory percussion"}], "description": "Why learn it: Students identify instruments, notation, and musical roles."}, {"id": "9d548f8d-0a5c-41cf-9d8c-408730ae6bff", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Logistics and setup", "children": [{"id": "1543865d-a57d-4d49-9485-e8d85e4679de", "type": "concept", "title": "Player count"}, {"id": "ebb22c06-b0f0-4e5e-aea3-e1d0b275e9df", "type": "concept", "title": "Instrument layout"}, {"id": "4ba41358-a95f-4495-85