n": "Why learn it: Students learn how register, dynamics, numbers of players, and instrumental projection affect audibility."}, {"id": "b3f79daf-7203-4c1d-b8a5-1e1dfc668a9c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Family integration", "children": [{"id": "ea234688-6fad-408b-a07e-f936d3d057ca", "type": "concept", "title": "Layering"}, {"id": "00dbacbe-8c2e-4448-93e8-d77aa222489a", "type": "concept", "title": "Handoffs"}, {"id": "84801e21-9101-4112-a4b5-ee5aa9b30fa9", "type": "concept", "title": "Choir contrast"}, {"id": "5a7bada9-d1ce-4b50-8eba-668d1bcabe4b", "type": "concept", "title": "Tutti writing"}, {"id": "be832f27-5b6d-4d70-8c18-3dd8da4b58e0", "type": "concept", "title": "Transparent scoring"}], "description": "Why learn it: Students practice combining strings, winds, brass, and percussion without overcrowding."}, {"id": "cb3d9bad-b63d-4d5c-9ca6-14609d9fc3ea", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Large-scale orchestral pacing", "children": [{"id": "30734dbe-8e6d-4212-9d0d-0158fb36b00d", "type": "concept", "title": "Builds"}, {"id": "ac18250d-4a0f-40db-9e54-546a40297c70", "type": "concept", "title": "Thinning"}, {"id": "87d08e8b-e3b5-4e2b-ac7c-f61ff4a75012", "type": "concept", "title": "Climaxes"}, {"id": "cfb0ff81-8d98-4eb5-a7c2-29a6be620524", "type": "concept", "title": "Cadential color"}, {"id": "d22cf58e-2089-4302-b96e-9ee7164d3471", "type": "concept", "title": "Reorchestration of returns"}], "description": "Why learn it: Students learn how orchestration shapes form over time."}]}, {"id": "cda3acec-7dcc-4d29-886d-4f2c18adca25", "type": "topic", "title": "Voicing and Doubling", "description": "Voicing and doubling determine whether an arrangement sounds clear, muddy, powerful, thin, blended, or colorful. Students learn to control vertical spacing and instrumental reinforcement.", "children": [{"id": "698c63e0-2a75-40e3-9a6b-77aef409f9ea", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Chord spacing", "children": [{"id": "6bee240d-cf0b-4da6-9e37-ef84b0a640d7", "type": "concept", "title": "Close position"}, {"id": "d9cc0352-a6c3-407b-9791-89c62571fa81", "type": "concept", "title": "Open position"}, {"id": "aa40c0ec-9abe-4db3-a6a4-9957c43c48ac", "type": "concept", "title": "Drop voicings"}, {"id": "13f295ee-51d6-4fba-ab69-16e78a4abaf2", "type": "concept", "title": "Low-interval limits"}, {"id": "33562041-99c4-42df-b4a5-d930d095ac22", "type": "concept", "title": "Register distribution"}], "description": "Why learn it: Students learn how spacing changes balance, clarity, and color."}, {"id": "64f728c5-990b-498b-8119-4435617241e8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Doubling strategies", "children": [{"id": "38198146-596d-4708-b306-e73c82697f4e", "type": "concept", "title": "Unison doubling"}, {"id": "8e8485a5-05b7-450d-b01b-86bd9475cb02", "type": "concept", "title": "Octave doubling"}, {"id": "b49eb6d9-4957-462b-b2e3-1b82f376d574", "type": "concept", "title": "Color doubling"}, {"id": "368f9334-4d59-49ec-98b3-f8d8bea50f89", "type": "concept", "title": "Avoiding clutter"}, {"id": "8cc1d721-fd49-4eec-870b-54af5374600b", "type": "concept", "title": "Doubling melody vs. harmony"}], "description": "Why learn it: Students practice doubling for color, reinforcement, blend, or emphasis."}, {"id": "ca3bbb8f-1404-40e3-a48c-680ce9ba0e49", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Reduction and expansion", "children": [{"id": "3ade2a10-f66b-4bd2-9b57-8a71db659482", "type": "concept", "title": "Piano texture analysis"}, {"id": "6683def0-2e68-4d0b-8ed2-20b7e56e8836", "type": "concept", "title": "Essential voices"}, {"id": "a4e165f1-a3e3-4eda-ab98-3236a3e78394", "type": "concept", "title": "Inner-line preservation"}, {"id": "77353cd5-6199-42ab-a803-6c4d87efbfef", "type": "concept", "title": "Expansion choices"}, {"id": "39c695d1-b302-4601-a6a9-39af31264fb4", "type": "concept", "title": "Recomposition boundaries"}], "description": "Why learn it: Students learn to move between piano reductions, chamber settings, and larger ensembles."}]}, {"id": "5260e92a-2b14-4331-9054-9005c5cf8c36", "type": "topic", "title": "Texture and Color", "description": "Texture and color are the expressive heart of orchestration. Students learn to shape density, transparency, motion, register, articulation, and timbre as compositional parameters.", "children": [{"id": "447153b1-3e37-43ee-a4bd-d1ee34d38814", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Texture types", "children": [{"id": "3662762b-418e-4791-8637-57f065e6fb45", "type": "concept", "title": "Melody and accompaniment"}, {"id": "27587860-94e5-486c-8834-b453ee17dad9", "type": "concept", "title": "Homophony"}, {"id": "e639051f-bd77-4c72-9a88-d298bef7b159", "type": "concept", "title": "Counterpoint"}, {"id": "9631d932-0fdd-4927-b22b-49e2796d9b82", "type": "concept", "title": "Ostinato layers"}, {"id": "28ddb8b7-fc13-45ca-b98f-d21486f9c7c8", "type": "concept", "title": "Massed sonority"}], "description": "Why learn it: Students identify and create common orchestral textures."}, {"id": "1b9df1aa-865c-4490-99f2-910052f77d34", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Color planning", "children": [{"id": "8d942a56-31c8-43e7-b2f2-a5ac079cceb3", "type": "concept", "title": "Color contrast"}, {"id": "9387d820-d924-4e96-a998-48a54d531ca8", "type": "concept", "title": "Gradual transformation"}, {"id": "96aa0ff2-14a4-46da-b9c7-9ec290fd008d", "type": "concept", "title": "Register migration"}, {"id": "2a4fa93e-ab37-473f-801b-983e879ee2c7", "type": "concept", "title": "Mute changes"}, {"id": "d93d0158-bb88-4752-9213-ae97dc4f5d61", "type": "concept", "title": "Timbre as form"}], "description": "Why learn it: Students learn to plan timbral change across phrases and sections."}, {"id": "d23e8d79-afc2-4b72-9d0f-39cc9286fb99", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Orchestral effects and extended techniques", "children": [{"id": "50d81b37-059f-491f-b021-2ca8837ac9af", "type": "concept", "title": "Sul ponticello"}, {"id": "b414e576-e5a6-4822-b7c7-1d9f71d01f09", "type": "concept", "title": "Flutter tongue"}, {"id": "7b0a45bc-67d4-4774-bc61-64fd34be6dd7", "type": "concept", "title": "Brass effects"}, {"id": "1dcfb614-635c-4149-90b7-15482c1906a9", "type": "concept", "title": "Percussion effects"}, {"id": "407e9252-0e93-4fa0-9735-4cdc9b054150", "type": "concept", "title": "Notation clarity"}], "description": "Why learn it: Students learn when special effects are musically useful and how to notate them responsibly."}]}, {"id": "8b0c4228-b5e4-4b0b-bccc-1c5673e5ba41", "type": "topic", "title": "Arranging for Various Ensembles", "description": "Arranging asks students to adapt musical ideas to new forces, contexts, and players. Students learn to preserve musical identity while making idiomatic choices for the target ensemble.", "children": [{"id": "c741717c-f613-49c1-b789-b918b78fdfa7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Small ensemble arranging", "children": [{"id": "03beddc5-c35a-4c70-9bff-c953b853def5", "type": "concept", "title": "Duos and trios"}, {"id": "36f59fbe-7499-4e8e-a7ed-c5405034f39e", "type": "concept", "title": "Quartets"}, {"id": "a2e57253-8418-437a-aa13-60f32ba62640", "type": "concept", "title": "Chamber winds"}, {"id": "52b79a26-e225-4d1b-93fe-82285f1055a7", "type": "concept", "title": "Rhythm section"}, {"id": "8105f4d0-b582-4f51-a6a9-d1d00279915c", "type": "concept", "title": "Educational ensembles"}], "description": "Why learn it: Students learn how to distribute essential material when forces are limited."}, {"id": "f09055e9-357c-4a65-bce7-70d94da07490", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Band, jazz, and commercial contexts", "children": [{"id": "4d1ac6e0-b2ba-4bd6-ad82-0fdc98fcb2c1", "type": "concept", "title": "Concert band"}, {"id": "80c760fb-1750-493f-bf85-6a60411e5aad", "type": "concept", "title": "Big band"}, {"id": "a65fb394-b7f9-46a7-b4c9-980225c6f28a", "type": "concept", "title": "Lead sheets"}, {"id": "0ece94a1-106f-4330-bb26-cecaabfd2b8c", "type": "concept", "title": "Horn section writing"}, {"id": "2c421b7e-b469-41ca-99df-121b7dfcb04c", "type": "concept", "title": "Pop rhythm section"}], "description": "Why learn i